ncy point Republican, and every major rater calls the race Lean or Likely R, with markets pricing Finstad near 74%. But two recent polls show Johnson tied or slightly ahead and he leads in fundraising, so the race stays competitive rather than comfortable for the incumbent.", "watch": "Whether the October polling tightening holds through Election Day, or whether the ad dispute over the alleged AI-fabricated spot shifts momentum.", "confidence": "medium", "notes": ["Incumbent Brad Finstad (R) is running."]}, "overview": "Southern Minnesota's 1st District pairs a Republican-leaning electorate with incumbent Brad Finstad, giving the GOP a structural edge. Expert raters uniformly place the race at Lean or Likely Republican, and prediction markets give Finstad roughly a three-in-four chance of holding the seat. The fundamentals model similarly points to a narrow Republican edge once incumbency and the district's partisan lean are weighed.\n\nStill, the race has tightened. A SurveyUSA poll in early October showed Jake Johnson up two, and a Democratic-sponsored poll in September had him up one, while Johnson has out-raised Finstad and holds comparable cash on hand. A headline dispute over a Finstad ad Johnson calls an AI fake has kept the contest in the news. The combination suggests a genuinely competitive race that Finstad still enters favored.", "history": [{"date": "2026-09-22", "p_dem": 0.1904, "margin": -5.38}, {"date": "2026-09-23", "p_dem": 0.19, "margin": -6.5}, {"date": "2026-09-24", "p_dem": 0.1925, "margin": -6.0}, {"date": "2026-09-25", "p_dem": 0.3207, "margin": -3.5}, {"date": "2026-09-26", "p_dem": 0.2388, "margin": -4.0}, {"date": "2026-09-27", "p_dem": 0.2075, "margin": -4.5}, {"date": "2026-09-28", "p_dem": 0.271, "margin": -4.0}, {"date": "2026-09-29", "p_dem": 0.3469, "margin": -3.0}, {"date": "2026-09-30", "p_dem": 0.2769, "margin": -4.0}, {"date": "2026-10-01", "p_dem": 0.2837, "margin": -4.0}, {"date": "2026-10-02", "p_dem": 0.2792, "margin": -4.0},